<BaseLayout title={page.title} hreflang={hreflang} description={page.description} canonical={page.canonical} ogType="article">
  <article class="page-content">
    <h1 class="page-title">{page.h1}</h1>
    
    <div class="entry-content" set:html={`<p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> May 8, 2026<br><strong>Last Updated:</strong> May 8, 2026</p><p>Welcome to Aviantestpro (&#8220;Company,&#8221; &#8220;we,&#8221; &#8220;our,&#8221; or &#8220;us&#8221;). This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, process, and protect your information when you access or use the website, services, products, applications, forms, laboratory testing services, online ordering systems, customer support channels, and related platforms operated by Aviantestpro (collectively, the “Services”).</p><p>This Privacy Policy is designed to comply with international privacy standards and applicable regulations, including:</p><ul><li>General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)</li><li>UK GDPR</li><li>California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA)</li><li>Singapore Personal Data Protection Act (PDPA)</li><li>Other applicable international privacy and consumer protection laws</li></ul><p>By accessing or using our Services, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>1. Who We Are</h2><p>Aviantestpro provides laboratory testing services, genetic testing solutions, avian diagnostics, molecular biology services, research-related products, laboratory consumables, testing kits, scientific information, and related customer support services for global customers.</p><p>If you have any questions regarding this Privacy Policy or your personal data, you may contact us at:</p><p><strong>Email:</strong> <a><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="d3b2b7bebabd93b2a5bab2bda7b6a0a7a3a1bcfdb0bcbe">[email&#160;protected]</span></a><br><strong>Website:</strong> <a>https://aviantestpro.com</a></p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>2. Information We Collect</h2><p>We may collect the following categories of information depending on how you interact with our Services.</p><h3>2.1 Personal Information You Provide</h3><p>We may collect information you voluntarily provide, including:</p><ul><li>Full name</li><li>Company or organization name</li><li>Email address</li><li>Telephone number</li><li>Shipping and billing address</li><li>Country or region</li><li>Payment-related information</li><li>Laboratory submission details</li><li>Customer support communications</li><li>Account login credentials</li><li>Order and transaction information</li><li>Uploaded files, documents, reports, or sample information</li></ul><h3>2.2 Laboratory and Testing Information</h3><p>Depending on the services requested, we may collect:</p><ul><li>Sample identifiers</li><li>Species information</li><li>Diagnostic information</li><li>Genetic testing data</li><li>Laboratory result records</li><li>Test history and associated metadata</li></ul><p>We process such information solely for legitimate laboratory, scientific, quality-control, operational, customer-support, and regulatory purposes.</p><h3>2.3 Automatically Collected Information</h3><p>When you visit our website, we may automatically collect certain technical information, including:</p><ul><li>IP address</li><li>Browser type and version</li><li>Device identifiers</li><li>Operating system</li><li>Referring URLs</li><li>Website interaction behavior</li><li>Time zone settings</li><li>Access dates and times</li><li>Cookies and tracking data</li></ul><h3>2.4 Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h3><p>We may use:</p><ul><li>Cookies</li><li>Pixels</li><li>Analytics tools</li><li>Session tracking technologies</li><li>Advertising technologies</li></ul><p>These technologies help us:</p><ul><li>Improve website functionality</li><li>Analyze website performance</li><li>Understand visitor behavior</li><li>Enhance user experience</li><li>Prevent fraud and abuse</li><li>Deliver relevant marketing content</li></ul><p>You may disable cookies through your browser settings. However, some website features may not function properly.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2><p>We may use collected information for the following purposes:</p><ul><li>Providing laboratory testing services</li><li>Processing orders and payments</li><li>Delivering reports and results</li><li>Managing customer accounts</li><li>Responding to inquiries and support requests</li><li>Improving website performance and security</li><li>Conducting analytics and research</li><li>Fulfilling contractual obligations</li><li>Sending operational notifications</li><li>Sending marketing communications where permitted by law</li><li>Detecting fraud, misuse, or unauthorized activities</li><li>Complying with legal and regulatory obligations</li><li>Protecting our legal rights and business interests</li></ul><p>We only process personal information where we have a lawful basis to do so.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>4. Legal Bases for Processing (GDPR)</h2><p>For users located in the European Economic Area (EEA), United Kingdom, or similar jurisdictions, we process personal data based on one or more of the following legal grounds:</p><ul><li>Your consent</li><li>Performance of a contract</li><li>Compliance with legal obligations</li><li>Legitimate business interests</li><li>Protection of vital interests</li><li>Scientific or research-related purposes where legally permitted</li></ul><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>5. Sharing and Disclosure of Information</h2><p>We do not sell personal information.</p><p>We may share information with:</p><ul><li>Payment processors</li><li>Shipping and logistics providers</li><li>Laboratory partners and technical service providers</li><li>IT infrastructure and hosting providers</li><li>Analytics and security service providers</li><li>Regulatory authorities when legally required</li><li>Professional advisors, auditors, or legal counsel</li><li>Government agencies or law enforcement where required by applicable law</li></ul><p>All third-party providers are expected to maintain appropriate confidentiality and security standards.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>6. International Data Transfers</h2><p>Because Aviantestpro serves international customers, your information may be transferred to and processed in countries outside your country of residence.</p><p>Where required by law, we implement appropriate safeguards for international data transfers, including:</p><ul><li>Standard contractual clauses</li><li>Data processing agreements</li><li>Secure transfer mechanisms</li><li>Commercially reasonable security safeguards</li></ul><p>By using our Services, you acknowledge that your information may be transferred internationally.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>7. Data Retention</h2><p>We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary to:</p><ul><li>Provide requested services</li><li>Maintain laboratory records</li><li>Fulfill contractual obligations</li><li>Resolve disputes</li><li>Comply with legal, tax, accounting, or regulatory requirements</li><li>Protect our legitimate business interests</li></ul><p>Retention periods may vary depending on the nature of the information and applicable legal obligations.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>8. Data Security</h2><p>We implement commercially reasonable technical, organizational, and administrative safeguards designed to protect your information, including:</p><ul><li>Secure servers and hosting infrastructure</li><li>Access controls and authentication systems</li><li>Encrypted communications where appropriate</li><li>Internal confidentiality measures</li><li>Monitoring against unauthorized access or misuse</li></ul><p>However, no method of transmission or storage is completely secure. Therefore, we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>9. Your Privacy Rights</h2><p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the following rights:</p><ul><li>Access your personal information</li><li>Correct inaccurate information</li><li>Request deletion of your information</li><li>Restrict or object to processing</li><li>Withdraw consent</li><li>Request data portability</li><li>Opt out of certain marketing communications</li><li>Lodge complaints with relevant supervisory authorities</li></ul><p>To exercise your rights, contact:</p><p><strong>Email:</strong> <a><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="68090c05010628091e0109061c0d1b1c181a07460b0705">[email&#160;protected]</span></a></p><p>We may require identity verification before processing certain requests.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>10. California Privacy Rights (CCPA/CPRA)</h2><p>If you are a California resident, you may have additional rights under California law, including:</p><ul><li>Right to know what personal information is collected</li><li>Right to request deletion</li><li>Right to correct inaccurate personal information</li><li>Right to opt out of certain data sharing practices</li><li>Right to non-discrimination for exercising privacy rights</li></ul><p>Aviantestpro does not sell personal information as defined under the CCPA/CPRA.</p><p>California residents may submit privacy requests by contacting:</p><p><strong>Email:</strong> <a><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="8efefce7f8efedf7ceeff8e7efe0faebfdfafefce1a0ede1e3">[email&#160;protected]</span></a></p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>11. GDPR and UK GDPR Rights</h2><p>If you are located in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, you may have rights under applicable data protection laws, including:</p><ul><li>Right of access</li><li>Right to rectification</li><li>Right to erasure</li><li>Right to restriction of processing</li><li>Right to data portability</li><li>Right to object</li><li>Rights related to automated decision-making</li></ul><p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>12. Marketing Communications</h2><p>We may send newsletters, product updates, technical notices, promotional information, or educational content where permitted by law.</p><p>You may unsubscribe at any time by:</p><ul><li>Clicking the unsubscribe link in emails</li><li>Contacting us directly</li><li>Adjusting account communication preferences</li></ul><p>Operational or service-related communications may still be sent when necessary.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>13. Third-Party Services and External Links</h2><p>Our website may contain links to third-party websites, applications, or services.</p><p>We are not responsible for:</p><ul><li>Third-party privacy practices</li><li>External website content</li><li>Third-party security measures</li><li>External data handling activities</li></ul><p>We encourage users to review the privacy policies of third-party services before interacting with them.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>14. Children&#8217;s Privacy</h2><p>Our Services are not intended for children under the age required by applicable law in their jurisdiction.</p><p>We do not knowingly collect personal information from children without appropriate legal authorization.</p><p>If you believe that a child has provided personal information to us, please contact us immediately.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>15. Automated Decision-Making</h2><p>We generally do not use fully automated decision-making processes that produce legal or similarly significant effects on users.</p><p>If this changes in the future, we will update this Privacy Policy accordingly.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>16. Do Not Track Signals</h2><p>Some browsers offer “Do Not Track” settings. Because there is currently no universally accepted standard for responding to such signals, our website may not respond to all Do Not Track requests.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>17. Website Analytics and Advertising</h2><p>We may use third-party analytics and advertising providers, including services such as:</p><ul><li>Google Analytics</li><li>Search Console tools</li><li>Advertising conversion tracking tools</li><li>Performance monitoring platforms</li></ul><p>These services may use cookies or similar technologies to collect information about website interactions.</p><p>Users may manage advertising preferences through browser or platform settings.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>18. Search Engine and AI Crawlers</h2><p>Our public website content may be indexed by:</p><ul><li>Search engines</li><li>AI search systems</li><li>Automated crawlers</li><li>Web indexing technologies</li></ul><p>Publicly available website content may appear in search results, AI-generated summaries, indexing databases, or similar discovery systems.</p><p>Private customer submissions, laboratory records, and confidential information are not intentionally published for public indexing.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/><h2>19. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2><p>We may update this Privacy Policy periodically.</p><p>When changes are made, we will revise</p><p></p></div>`} />
